{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T18:25:18.408Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "The kernel half of e63909ba. evolve uses each event's :event/at as the now it evaluates guards against (stage.cljc), so a forward-dated event satisfies :elapsed-since at that instant and a sticky stage locks the reach in permanently - unreachable by retraction. Clamping at our own write boundary does not help for events that arrive from another replica already postdated. The options each cost something: clamp evolve's now against the caller-supplied now (changes derivation for existing logs), require a witnessed clock for time guards on sticky stages (needs witness infrastructure, ADR 0012), or accept it and surface future-dated events in every lens. Wants an ADR and a PLAN 19 verdict, not a patch."} :event/parents #{"sha256-7f7bb660ecfb5e1453940b444cc0c2deb2603f4c7a9becef92f9feb9c58a60be"} :event/ticket #uuid "1cdd877e-cf48-40be-8bc5-2603bb94ce0e" :event/type :fact/assert}